anslate(2833.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\" transform=\"translate(833,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Therefore, the correct thickness of the sheet is 1.54 mm. \n<br><br>Hence, the correct option is (A).</p>","exam":"jee-main","questions":[{"question_id":"pin-a-screw-gauge-the-zero-of-the-circular-scale-lies-3-d-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-jis8h2tqloupzyk0","qKey":"pin-a-screw-gauge-the-zero-of-the-circular-scale-lies-3-d-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-jis8h2tqloupzyk0","permalink":"pin-a-screw-gauge-the-zero-of-the-circular-scale-lies-3-d-jee-main-physics-units-and-measurements-jis8h2tqloupzyk0","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2026 (Online) 23rd January Morning Shift","year":2026,"subject":"physics","chapter":"units-and-measurements","type":"mcq","marks":4,"negMarks":1,"content":"<p>In a screw gauge, the zero of the circular scale lies 3 divisions above the horizontal pitch line when their metallic studs are brought in contact. Using this instrument thickness of a sheet is measured. If pitch scale reading is 1 mm and the circular scale reading is 51 then the correct thickness of the sheet is <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.14ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.525ex\" height=\"0.084ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 25 2000 37\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1000,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(1500,0)\"><use data-c=\"5F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5F\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> mm.</p>\n<p>[Assume least count is 0.01 mm ]</p>\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"<p>1.54</p>\n"},{"identifier":"B","content":"<p>1.50</p>\n"},{"identifier":"C","content":"<p>1.51</p>\n"},{"identifier":"D","content":"<p>1.48</p>"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>The circular scale lies 3 divisions above the horizontal pitch line when the studs are in contact.</p>\n<p>When the zero mark is above the reference line, the screw has been turned past the zero point. This indicates a negative zero error. The error corresponds to 3 divisions.</p>\n<p>Hence, the zero error is,</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.566ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"64.12ex\" height=\"2.262ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -750 28341.1 1000\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"45\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-45\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(714,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1395.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(2451.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(3229.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(3618.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4340.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\" transform=\"translate(5340.6,0)\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0Least Count\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(13140.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(13807.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(14863.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(15641.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"28\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-28\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(16030.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"33\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-33\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16752.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(17752.6,0)\"><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\"></use><use data-c=\"2E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2E\" transform=\"translate(500,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"30\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-30\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"></use><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\" transform=\"translate(1278,0)\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(19530.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mtext\" style=\"font-family: Roboto,'Tiro Devanagari Hindi','Tiro Bangla',sans-serif;\"><text data-variant=\"-explicitFont\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\" font-size=\"884px\">\u00a0</text></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(600,0)\"><use data-c=\"6D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-6D\"></use><use data-c